label version_08:

    narrator "\[ VERSION 0.8 - Crunch \]"
    pause 0.5
    narrator "The world starts showing its exhaustion."

    narrator "Tuesday happens twice. Not the same Tuesday — different weather, different light. Same date on the calendar."
    narrator "You check. Nobody else does."

    narrator "Two bakeries appear on the same street. Identical, down to the crack in the second window from the left."
    narrator "You work in both of them. You don't remember moving between them."

    narrator "The mayor starts saying things that don't belong to him."

    mayor "Clara always said the morning light here was something special."
    narrator "He stops. Something crosses his face."
    mayor "I've always loved the morning light here."
    narrator "He walks away. You write the name in your notebook before you can forget it. The ink holds."

    narrator "Then she appears in the bakery doorway."
    narrator "Her face. Her voice. But the eyes are off — too still, tracking nothing."

    mina "Merge conflict."
    narrator "She blinks."
    mina "Fixed memory leak."
    narrator "She blinks again."
    mina "Temporary solution. Will address in next build."
    narrator "She turns and walks away. You follow her around a corner."
    narrator "She's gone.

    $ notebook_entries.append("clara. the mayor said her name. 'clara always said the morning light was something special.' then caught himself. her name was clara.")
    $ notebook_entries.append("mina was in the bakery doorway. said 'merge conflict.' 'fixed memory leak.' eyes were wrong. not her.")
    $ show_notebook_icon = True

    jump version_09
